project: Task game-monsters blocked: The task itself is implemented and verified, but its acceptance (`npm test` exits 0) cannot be met from inside my file scope. Three pre-existing assertions assert the pre-monster world and are each broken by the contract I was told to implement, in files I may not edit:

1. test/game-combat.test.js:121 asserts `game.act({ type: 'pickup' })` returns exactly ['You pick up the Dagger.'], but the fixture places a goblin on (3,2) next to the player on (2,2) and pickup costs a turn, so the goblin legitimately attacks: ['You pick up the Dagger.', 'The goblin hits you for 2.'].
2. test/game-combat.test.js:168 asserts `state.log.at(-1) === 'You hit the goblin for 4.'`; the adjacent goblin's counter-attack is now the newest log line. Its own comment says the monster phase "is not asserted here", but .at(-1) does assert it.
3. test/game-world.test.js:313 and :315 assert every monster is still outside room 0 (and never adjacent to the player) after `game.act({ type: 'descend' })`; the brief and design §5 both say descend costs a turn and "the new level's monsters act once", so a monster placed within its sight of the player can step into room 0 or up beside the player on that same turn.

There is no implementation that satisfies both the contract ("when the action costs a turn ... every monster takes its turn", with the adjacent monster attacking) and these assertions, so the fixtures/assertions need updating. Please widen my scope to those two test files or add a follow-up task for them: (1) assert the leading message (or move the fixture's goblin out of the room), (2) assert messages[0] / the player's hp instead of the log tail, (3) assert the placement invariants on the freshly generated level before the descend turn's monster phase, or relax them to the invariants that still hold (no shared tiles, monsters on floor, monsters never on the player)..
