project: Task undo-core blocked: npm test cannot go green from inside this task's file scope. test/game-world.test.js:709, in the test 'applyKey: keys that are not actions return null', still asserts that 'z' is not a key: `for (const key of ['x', 'z', 'Z', '0', '?', 'i', ' ', '\\n', '', 'R', 'M', 'hh'])`. Phase 2 requires the opposite — applyKey(game, 'z') must return ['You rewind time.'] or ['Nothing to rewind.'], never null — so that assertion is now necessarily false and is the single remaining failure in the suite (188 pass, 1 fail). test/game-world.test.js is outside this task's file scope (the Edit tool refuses it), no planned task owns it (game-world, game-combat, game-monsters and core-tests are all done), and task_split rejects children whose files fall outside the parent scope, so I cannot hand the fix off either. The blocker is one line, not a design problem: remove 'z' from that array (keeping 'Z', the uppercase key, which is still not an action), and npm test is fully green. Nothing else in the suite assumes 'z' is dead — the neighbouring runScript test spells its noise with uppercase 'Z'. Suggested fix paths: add test/game-world.test.js to undo-core's scope and re-run it (everything else in the task is already done on disk), or add a one-line task owning that file, ordered before undo-render/undo-page, which depend on undo-core being green..
